WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:06.020
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.120
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.700
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:26.470
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:34.210
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.680
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.550
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.290
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.950
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.630
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.630 --> 00:01:01.700
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.680
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:12.320
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.220
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.460
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:32.570
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:37.310
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.040
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.880
<i>Narumi-san...</i>

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.520
You have three choices.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.600
An explosion caused by my bomb,

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.060
an explosion caused
by static electricity,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.400
or...

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.270
...complete surrender to me...

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.540
<i>Well, Ayumu-kun?
It's up to you to decide.</i>

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.220
<i>He's not like the
other Blade Children...</i>

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.340
<i>He's not testing me...</i>

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.120
<i>He'll do whatever it takes to beat me,</i>

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.760
<i>no matter the consequences...</i>

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.120
<i>He really wants me dead!</i>

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.260
<i>No matter what happens,</i>

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.390
<i>I just know you'll
be able to overcome it...</i>

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:49.630
<i>Believe in yourself!</i>

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.980
"The Sound of an Iris
Freezing and Melting"

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.910
The shoddy light of hope does nothing

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.810
but confuse people.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.340
<i>Wouldn't you agree, Ayumu-kun?</i>

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.220
To be honest, I'm at my rope's end.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.320
If I can be saved by conceding to you,

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.760
then I won't hesitate to
kneel down and dirty my forehead.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.260
In that case...

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:19.130
You said I have three choices...

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:25.170
But in actuality,
I've only been given one.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.940
If you're going along
with my brother's rule,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.040
then only death should await the loser.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.040
In other words,
conceding to you won't save me.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.610
It'll be "the end".

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.610
Is that your conclusion?

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.620
Yeah.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.190
Either way, I have no choice
but to kneel down pitifully.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:46.660
In which case,
can I have one last request?

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.690
-A request?
-Yes...

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:52.660
Sure, let's hear it.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:55.430
I want you to spare Madoka.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:59.160
It would pain me to have
someone die because of me...

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:05.140
Certainly, I have no
qualms with sparing her...

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.210
However...

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:10.410
Your flimsy lie about kneeling
down before me is pathetic...

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.650
<i>Drop the act, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.020
There is a single spot within
everyone where light resides.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.020
Do you know where?

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.110
The eyes.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.560
The light of resistance
still resides in your eyes.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.730
It refutes your words and
insists that no, you will not die.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.710
Am I wrong?

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:42.680
For someone so high-handed,
you sure don't act it.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.780
Your ability to throw
my thinking off balance

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.680
at a time like this impresses me.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.120
<i>But there's no point in
planning anything, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.660
Everyone's eyes have me
in a mount position.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.590
Then why do you hesitate?

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:59.900
You hold so much conviction

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.630
and stand in such an
advantageous position,

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:07.240
so why do you fret before
such a petty light of hope?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.940
"It's very small, but within me

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.480
there is still hesitation about
if it's really okay to lose you."

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.810
Is that what you want me to say?

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.310
<i>Unfortunately, that's not the case,
Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.450
I'm aware of that.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:25.550
Your aim is to completely deny
the meaning of my existence.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:29.260
In other words, you don't have
a single expectation of me.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:33.090
<i>But you do have fear. Am I wrong?</i>

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.600
It's not much, but you
fear this minuscule light.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.030
Isn't that right?

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.770
Your ability to firmly
believe in yourself

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.710
<i>just before you die impresses me,
Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:50.450
I have no expectations of myself.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.280
Not once in my entire life
have I ever felt

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.880
the meaning of my own existence.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:59.450
I wouldn't even be needed
if my brother were here...

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:02.490
But even so...

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:05.150
...I cannot completely
give up on myself!

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:08.000
Even if I don't know
if I'll live or not,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.730
I have no choice but to try!

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:13.390
You wish to believe in yourself,
is that it?

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:18.930
Then try. Believe in your foolish self.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:47.740
There's not a single element
here to bring you victory.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:52.310
There is no escape from this
huge pile of explosives.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.740
Even if you do try and escape,

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.510
the static electricity will
unquestionably set off an explosion.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.750
Three minutes after
I press this button

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:09.850
you will realize just how
powerless you really are.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:15.560
You're truly pitiable.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.870
<i>I shall take Madoka-san
to a safe place.</i>

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.130
<i>Farewell, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:46.520
May you disappear
with your false hope...

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.300
<i>Ayumu!</i>

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.390
How?!

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:24.260
This.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:38.410
So you fought a bomb with a bomb...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.580
Thanks to this bomb of yours,

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.950
I was able to delay the blast
for a brief instant.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:06.440
And thanks to that short delay,

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.930
I was able to escape unharmed.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:14.850
Though you might've called it
the light of a reckless hope.

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:20.850
I'll be leaving now.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.050
She's at the bridge nearby.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.230
You're a frightening man.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:32.170
Despite having the look of a loser,

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.200
you continue to believe in possibility.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:39.210
I never once imagined
you had taken that.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.640
If you don't give up,

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.110
possibility will
always be around you.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.410
The "happiness of those who believe"...

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:49.210
<i>That is what irises signify...</i>

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:58.450
Resourcefulness and the
strength to believe in yourself...

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.430
But don't you think there is something

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:04.800
that can shatter those
things in an instant?

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:10.000
Yes! Nothing beats extreme violence!

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:19.940
When was it that we started
down different paths?

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:29.720
You were the one who chose
the path of recklessness, Eyes.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.490
Even so, there is hope.

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.330
Hope for what?

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:38.170
Should we continue to live
in the darkness of despair...

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:42.370
...as long as we exist,
all we can do is have faith

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.130
that the meaning of
our existence lies within.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:05.490
Our fate is not that simple, Eyes.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:08.660
Kiyotaka's "happiness
of those who believe"

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.730
does not exist in our world!

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:16.140
How long are you guys
going to quote my brother?!

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.070
I've had enough.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.110
I can only do what I can.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:28.410
That's all.

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:37.890
That's all?

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:42.920
That's all it took to triumph over me?

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:05.620
Ayumu!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.090
Ayumu!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.320
Are you alright?

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:14.190
I should be asking you!
You're all covered in ash!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:18.170
Madoka...I...

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.130
I can't do anything...

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.970
Don't say it, Ayumu...

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.110
I'm so sorry!

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.530
Alright...

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.380
Hello? Hello?!

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.780
<i>Eyes-kun! Is it really you?!</i>

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:23.030
No, I'm not crying...

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.960
Ayumu...

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.400
Ayumu!

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:01.570
How long are you gonna sleep?
It's morning already!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:02.740
Madoka?

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:06.540
Go wash up. Breakfast is ready.

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:14.780
What are you doing?
Eat before it gets cold!

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.680
Yeah...

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.820
There's still more soup. Want some?

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.980
Yeah...

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:28.560
It just doesn't seem right...

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.930
Eh? What doesn't?

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:33.430
<i>No, I just can't believe
you're making me breakfast...</i>

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.040
How rude!

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.010
I can make something this simple too,
you know!

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.810
That's not what I meant...

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:44.280
I guess maybe I'm a little happy...

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.180
How cute of you to say that!

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:48.480
Go ahead and eat up!

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.680
But actually...

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:53.860
...you're going to be late!

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:56.090
Why didn't you say so sooner?!

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:58.580
-See you later!
-Bye!

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:12.740
<i>Narumi-san! Good morning!</i>

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:14.000
Morning.

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:17.880
-What?
-Oh, nothing!

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:22.720
That reminds me,
thanks for yesterday...

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:23.590
The truth is...

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:24.590
No, that's okay!

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:28.260
All that matters is
that I was useful to you!

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.590
Yeah...

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.190
You really helped me out a lot...

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:34.130
Didn't I, though?!

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:36.930
-And your rice ball, too.
-My rice ball?

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:41.300
Ryoko!

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:44.770
Yo!

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.950
-Kosuke...
-Yeah?

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:59.590
What's going to happen to us?

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:01.790
What do you mean?

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:06.560
We carry a burden that's
too heavy to do anything about...

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.730
What do we do now?

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.290
Run.

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:15.370
Run. Run as much as you can!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:18.040
I'll watch you as you do.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.910
Run, Ryoko.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.440
Kosuke...

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:26.500
-That's sassy, even for you!
-Ow!

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.860
Hey, Rio!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:35.090
Want a ride?

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.590
<i>Ryoko-chan! Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:42.190
<i>Guess what?! Eyes-kun came back!</i>

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:50.040
It looks like all the
Blade Children are back in school.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.270
I see...

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:53.680
Well, it's time for class,

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:56.110
what do you say we hit the books too?!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.310
<i>-I'll be sleeping on the roof.
-Narumi-san!</i>

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:02.110
-See you after school!
-Yeah.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:25.710
Wataya.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.240
I'm sorry, Assistant Inspector!

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.880
Tonight's not a good night!

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:33.450
And look at how thin my precious
little Wally has become!

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:36.250
Oh, how will we ever make it
through 'til payday?!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.490
What are you talking about?

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:41.820
Huh? What's with you,
Assistant Inspector?

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:43.320
What do you mean?

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:46.390
You're made up all fancy-like for once!

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:47.860
Did something happen?

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:50.630
Sort of. I'm thinking
of taking a vacation...

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.370
A vacation?! At a busy time like this?!

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:55.040
Are you going to a hot spring?

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.440
Something like that.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.770
Cover for me while I'm gone!

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:01.010
Yes, ma'am...

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:03.380
A hot spring sounds great...

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:06.210
It's warm out...

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:10.340
-It's spring now...
-That it is...

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:27.030
<i>I feel I understand
a little bit now...</i>

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.240
<i>The meaning behind
Kiyotaka Narumi's words...</i>

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.420
<i>Kanone...</i>

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:50.860
<i>Even if our paths differ...</i>

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:54.750
<i>The world we live in is but one...</i>

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:02.920
<i>Fate can't be changed.</i>

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.700
<i>Are you so sure?</i>

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:25.710
<i>Fate...</i>

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:30.050
<i>What is it?</i>

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:46.490
<i>A sweet scent washes
into my parched throat</i>

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:53.220
<i>and my feelings
continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:11.280
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:16.950
<i>that's like you're
following a soccer ball</i>

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:22.860
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:29.460
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:35.200
<i>Adults who talk about marriage
as penalty games</i>

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:40.310
<i>are children who can never dream...</i>

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:46.080
<i>Since you were able
to fall in love with me,</i>

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:52.590
<i>I'm sure the girl you chose is wonderful</i>

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:58.460
<i>Those days long ago when
we would talk about anything...</i>

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:03.600
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:09.340
<i>to have those slightly
awkward discussions about love</i>

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:15.170
<i>The more I wish
for everyone's happiness</i>

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:21.110
<i>the more picture postcards
there are of me and my husband</i>

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:26.920
<i>Your child that I wanted from the
bottom of my heart five years ago</i>

00:22:26.920 --> 00:22:33.150
<i>bears no resemblance to me</i>

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:36.200
Ayumu...

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:38.630
This is what I think...

00:22:38.630 --> 00:22:43.140
As long as you don't give up,
there will always be hope.

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:46.470
So I'm sure fate can be changed...

00:22:48.570 --> 00:22:50.910
<i>I'm sure it can, Madoka.</i>

00:22:52.150 --> 00:22:54.840
<i>I'm sure it can...</i>

00:22:56.720 --> 00:23:02.490
<i>There are many things
I love and dream about,</i>

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:07.590
<i>yet if I had pushed
just a little more today</i>

00:23:07.590 --> 00:23:13.430
<i>nothing would have come from it
but another "what-if" excuse...</i>

00:23:13.430 --> 00:23:19.240
<i>I won't need any nights of
drowning myself in a sweet cocktail</i>

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:24.940
<i>to escape my difficulties and sadness</i>

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:36.760
<i>I will escape into a drawn-out battle
with them once more</i>

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:48.500
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly</i>

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:54.210
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:23:54.210 --> 00:24:00.840
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:06.520
<i>Narumi-san! Over here!</i>

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:08.450
They're so pretty!

